DESCRIPTION:Still from THE FIXER\, directed by Mimi Chakarova and Lydia Ch
 ávez\n\nThe 29th United Nations Association Film Festival presents free p
 rogramming for kids on Saturday\, Oct. 17\, in Palo Alto\, featuring two s
 hort documentaries.\nThe program opens with the world premiere of “The F
 ixer\,” a 12-minute stop-motion documentary from local filmmakers Mimi C
 hakarova and Lydia Chávez. The film follows a 10-year-old girl determined
  to fix what is broken in a fragile world.\nThe program continues with “
 Under the Canopy\,” directed by Michal Krawczyk. Set in Colombia’s And
 ean-Amazon Piedmont\, the documentary follows a community-led effort to ma
 p biodiversity and restore forests while preserving Indigenous ecological 
 knowledge.\n\n**Admission is free.** This special UNAFF & Kids Program off
 ers an opportunity to see two short documentaries suitable for all audienc
 es. The 29th UNAFF runs Oct. 15-25\, 2026\, with the theme “Passion for 
 Change.” The festival features films addressing human rights issues\, in
 cluding the environment\, women’s rights\, racism and peace\, and engage
 s audiences throughout the Bay Area.\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.unaff
