UID:funcheap-1640852@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Movies
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerStill from THE DREAMING GAME\,
  directed by Jordan Salvatoriello.The 29th United Nations Association Film
  Festival presents a free shorts program on Sunday\, Oct. 18\, in Palo Alt
 o\, featuring three documentaries that explore wildlife conservation\, wro
 ngful incarceration\, and the global impact of cryptocurrency.\nThe progra
 m opens with “Crossing the Divide\,” directed and produced by local fi
 lmmaker Talia Frank. The 11-minute documentary examines how roads fragment
  wildlife habitats and explores the potential of wildlife crossings to res
 tore animal movement and strengthen ecosystems.\n\nNext is “The Dreaming
  Game\,” directed and produced by Jordan Salvatoriello. The film follows
  70-year-old Raymond Gaines\, a Boston native and lifelong baseball fan\, 
 as he returns to Fenway Park after spending 47 years in prison for a murde
 r he did not commit. As he awaits a decision on his case\, Gaines works to
  rebuild his life and pursue his long-sought freedom.\nThe program conclud
 es with “The Market and the Monkey’s Paw\,” directed and produced by
  “Graham New\, Leo Safir\, and Oliver Richards. Set in El Salvador\, the
  documentary explores the country’s adoption of Bitcoin as legal tender 
 through the perspectives of market vendors\, educators and community membe
 rs\, examining questions of economic inclusion\, tourism\, gentrification 
 and digital finance.\n**Admission is free.** The special program from UNAF
 F offers an opportunity to see three short documentaries and discover the.
 ..\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.unaff.org/2026/schedule.html\nDetails: 
 https://sf.funcheap.com/united-nations-association-film-festival-free-shor
 ts-program/\nSource: Funcheap SF
