DESCRIPTION:Between landing a promotion to cover artist at her queer activ
 ist zine to falling for her impossibly cool girlfriend (Samira Wiley\, The
  Handmaid’s Tale)\, Sarah (Abbi Jacobson\, Broad City) is finally hittin
 g her stride in ‘90s San Francisco. But a trip home to visit her oddball
  family upends everything. Sarah’s mom\, the once-vibrant Midge (Julia L
 ouis-Dreyfus\, Veep)\, isn’t herself — and Sarah’s father (Bryan Cra
 nston\, Breaking Bad) and sister (Beanie Feldstein\, Booksmart) aren’t q
 uite ready to see the concerning shifts.\n\nPulled between her exciting li
 fe in the Bay and being there for her mother\, Sarah tries to find her foo
 ting in a disorienting world — a world where Alzheimer’s disease is sl
 owly eroding Midge’s sense of self. Based on Sarah Leavitt’s graphic n
 ovel and featuring powerhouse performances from its award-winning ensemble
  cast\, which also includes Seth Rogen (The Studio)\, Wanda Sykes\, and Bo
 wen Yang (Fire Island)\, Leah Nelson’s animated directorial debut is an 
 achingly beautiful story of acceptance and a meditation on the relationshi
 ps that shape — and reshape — us.\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/eve
 nts/2026/10/20/frameline50-fall-showcase-tangles-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
