BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:B-Movie: Lust & Sound in West-Berlin
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T200000
DTSTAMP:20261018T205153Z
UID:funcheap-1642337@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Movies
DESCRIPTION:© DEF Media GmbHJoin us for a filmscreening of B-Movie: Lust 
 & Sound in West-Berlin:\nHoping to follow in the footsteps of legends like
  David Bowie and CAN\, Manchester punk rocker and early electronic music a
 colyte Mark Reeder arrives in a divided Berlin in 1979. Luckily\, he films
  everything he sees: black leather-clad teenagers\, giant pink and red hai
 rdos\, gritty basement gigs\, and a parade of the scene’s most illustrio
 us figures\, including Nick Cave\, Mania D’s Gudrun Gut\, and Einstürze
 nde Neubauten’s Blixa Bargeld. From the movement’s system-smashing hig
 hs to its waning years in the age of reunification\, Reeder is the outside
 r with an insider’s view of the beating heart of Germany’s underground
  cultural life.\nLovingly assembled from a decade of fascinating film and 
 audio material\, B-Movie: Lust & Sound in West-Berlin provides a fast-pace
 d but no less intimate look at Berlin’s punk and electronic subculture t
 hrough the eyes of one of its greatest devotees. Winner of the Heiner Caro
 w Prize at the 2015 Berlin International Film Festival.\n\nWith Mark Reede
 r\, Marius Weber\, Gudrun Gut\, Annette Humpe\, Blixa Bargeld\, Nick Cave\
 , Nena\, and Christiane F.\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.eventbrite.com/
 e/b-movie-lust-sound-in-west-berlin-tickets-2000526819570\nDetails: https:
 //sf.funcheap.com/bmovie-lust-sound-westberlin-sf/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Websit
 e-quer.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261018T205153Z
LOCATION:Goethe-Institut San Francisco\, 657 Howard Street San Francisco\,
  CA 94105
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/bmovie-lust-sound-westberlin-sf/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Filipiñana
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T223000
DTSTAMP:20261007T210655Z
UID:dothebay-17930193@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:Director Rafael Manuel in person for introduction and Q&A mode
 rated by Ali El-Sadany\, editor of FilmSlop\, on Saturday\, September 5 (a
 t rush).\n\nPresented by FiliKula\n\nAmid stifling heat and pervasive drou
 ght\, Isabel (Jorrybell Agoto)\, a 17-year-old Ilokana from the rural nort
 h\, works at a posh country club outside Manila\, lining up golf balls for
  powerful men to drive into the verdant horizon. New to the job\, she wand
 ers the immaculate grounds sampling its luxuries as members\, including an
  industrialist and his expatriate niece\, the club president and his pampe
 red wife\, and a slew of Chinese tourists\, engage in a complex dance with
  the club’s doting and subservient staff. But something is rotting benea
 th the pristine fairways of the elite resort\, as Isabel discovers when sh
 e tries to return a mislaid golf club to its patriarchal director\, Dr. Pa
 lanca (Teroy Guzman). The deeper she journeys into its most exclusive corn
 ers\, the closer she gets to the violent truths of the club\, her native P
 hilippines\, and her own past..\n\n“A masterwork…with Filipiñana\, Ma
 nuel opens new vistas in the future of the cinema.” – The New Yorker\n
 \n“An invigorating dose of arch formalism in a sea of mainstream sinceri
 ty\, this is the kind of movie that asks for the viewer’s attention…th
 e angle of a golf club can evoke suspense\, a piece of fruit on the ground
  can feel like a tragedy\, and a casual glance can take your breath away.
 ” – Vulture\n\nRuntime\n\n1h 40m\n\nYear\n\n2026\n\nDirector\n\nRafael
  Manuel\n\nFormat\n\nDCP...\n\nTickets: https://ticketing.uswest.veezi.com
 /purchase/22300?siteToken=4m48btf3yavn7xjk5yxk6nc40c\nDetails: https://dot
 hebay.com/events/2026/10/22/filipinana-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
