DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerCredit: Maxita producersCine+M
 ás SF Latino Film Festival & the San Francisco Public Library present MAX
 ITA.\nExperience the USA premiere of MAXITA\, a compelling documentary fro
 m Brazil directed by Mariana Machado and Ana Maria Machado. Through Indige
 nous perspectives\, environmental struggles\, and spiritual connections to
  the land\, the film explores the urgent fight to protect the planet and i
 ts natural resources.\n\nMaxita: Film screening & Panel Discussion\nSaturd
 ay\, October 31\, 2026 | 2-4p\nKoret Auditorium\, 100 Larkin St.\, SF\nFRE
 E – RSVP\nDirs. Mariana Machado\, Ana Maria Machado\, Brazil/Belgium\, 2
 026\, 70 mins runtime. C0-presented with the San Francisco Public Library\
 nVisit CineMasSF.org for details on other films screening at the festival.
 \nThe 18th Cine+Más San Francisco Latino Film Festival brings films from 
 across the U.S.\, Latin America and Spain to venues throughout San Francis
 co. This year’s lineup celebrates Latino stories and filmmakers through 
 documentaries\, dramas\, comedies and films exploring culture\, identity\,
  family\, migration and community.\nABOUT THE FILM\nMAXITA\nThe shaman Dav
 i Kopenawa Yanomami\, one of the most important voices of Brazil’s Indig
 enous peoples\, faces constant threats to his life as he embarks on a jour
 ney that takes him from the Amazon to the mining industry on the other sid
 e of the country\, where he reunites with his old friend Ailton Krenak. Th
 eir encounter sheds light on the ongoing devastation of Brazil’s forests
 ...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://cinemassf2026.eventive.org/schedule/maxita
 -6ac0484fdb9bd3936b57d8b1\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/free-cinems-fi
 lm-festival-maxita-usa-premiere-sf/\nSource: Funcheap SF
