BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Two Films. One Manilatown Legacy.
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T150000
DTSTAMP:20261020T194441Z
UID:dothebay-17914045@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:"Two Films. One Manilatown Legacy." brings two generations of 
 San Francisco's Manilatown and International Hotel history to the big scre
 en at SFMOMA for a special FREE double-feature presentation.\n\nAt 1 PM\, 
 experience the San Francisco premiere of the newly enhanced and restored e
 dition of Curtis Choy's landmark 1983 documentary\, "The Fall of the I-Hot
 el". The film chronicles the decade-long struggle to save San Francisco's 
 International Hotel and the August 4\, 1977 eviction of its predominantly 
 Filipino and Chinese elder tenants. Following the screening\, filmmaker Cu
 rtis Choy joins co-producers of the enhanced edition for a community conve
 rsation moderated by Caroline Ocampo.\n\nAt 3 PM\, experience the premiere
  of "Manilatown Manang"\, the story of Jeanette Gandionco Lazam-artist\, a
 ctivist\, and one of the few women who lived in the International Hotel as
  a Tenant Defender during the historic anti-eviction movement. The film fo
 llows Jeanette's journey from the I-Hotel struggle through a lifetime of a
 ctivism\, art\, and community. Following the premiere\, Jeanette Lazam joi
 ns the film's producers and creative team for a community conversation mod
 erated by Caroline Ocampo.\n\nTogether\, the films create a powerful dialo
 gue between past and present: audiences first encounter Jeanette as a youn
 g activist in Choy's historic documentary\, then experience the continuati
 on of her story in Manilatown Manang.\n\nSaturday\, November 7\, 2026\nSFM
 OMA - Phyllis Wattis Theater\n151 Third Street\, San Franc...\n\nFree\nMan
 ilatown Heritage Foundation\n\nTickets: https://www.manilatown.org/all-eve
 nts/two-films-one-manilatown-legacy\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/
 2026/11/7/two-films-one-manilatown-legacy-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay\n\nAls
 o listed on:\n- https://sf.funcheap.com/free-filipino-manilatown-film-doub
 le-feature-qas-sfmoma/
GEO:37.7859072;-122.4008003
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34760581/3819352f-b4f1-43ed-a343-2f1b06bcb32e.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261020T194441Z
LOCATION:SFMOMA\, 151 Third Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94103
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/7/two-films-one-manilatown-legacy-
 tickets
END:VEVENT
