SUMMARY:New People: A Deeper Love: The Story of Miss Peppermint
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T150000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17901314@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:All listed screenings take place at NEW PEOPLE CINEMA\, locate
 d at 1746 Post Street in Japantown.\n\nA Deeper Love: The Story of Miss Pe
 ppermint is an award-winning documentary that follows trailblazing perform
 er and activist Peppermint across nearly a decade of her life and career.\
 n\nMoving between intimate private moments and major public milestones\, t
 he documentary reveals the realities behind the spotlight: the struggle to
  survive as a working artist\, the pressure of becoming a symbol\, and the
  friendships and chosen family that sustain her along the way.\n\nAt its h
 eart\, A Deeper Love is a story about persistence\, chosen family\, and th
 e power of queer artists to shape culture while fighting to live authentic
 ally.\n\n“Powerful\, urgent\, and deeply human.” – Elliot Page\, The
  Hollywood Reporter\n\n“This documentary arrives at a time when Trans vo
 ices need to be heard the loudest.” – Attitude Magazine\n\nRuntime\n\n
 1h 26m\n\nYear\n\n2025\n\nDirector\n\nOriel Pe'er\n\nFormat\n\nDCP\n\nCoun
 try\n\nUSA\n\nFirst Showing\n\nNovember 22\, 2026\n\nCategories\n\nNew Peo
 ple Cinema\n\n\,\n\nFeatured\n\nTickets: https://ticketing.uswest.veezi.co
 m/purchase/22203?siteToken=b6y5tsmq2ayrxb4ymw2rah8wy0\nDetails: https://do
