BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pearl
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T213000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17915212@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:The allure of stardom on the big screen proves to be a road to
  some very dark places for Mia Goth’s titular PEARL in this stylish and 
 gruesome prequel to Ti West’s X. With her husband away at war\, Pearl fi
 nds herself dreaming of a way to escape from her boring life on the farm. 
 She sees the silver screen as her way to find stardom and the love she so 
 desperately needs\, but her overbearing mother and her own dark impulses m
 ight hold her back from the fame she craves.\n\nPEARL proves to be a delig
 htfully perverse study on a standout character from writer/director Ti Wes
 t’s tribute to ‘70s grindhouse\, X. Its vibrant\, candy-coated veneer 
 plays wonderfully against the depraved desires of the main character bubbl
 ing just below the surface. Co-writer/star Mia Goth gives another deliciou
 sly unhinged performance as Pearl\, a not-quite-innocent farm girl looking
  for love in all the wrong places. As much a love letter to the Golden Age
  of Hollywood as it is a demented look at the darkness bubbling just below
  the surface of rural America\, PEARL is colorful\, unnerving\, and twiste
 d in all the right ways.\n\nTickets: https://drafthouse.com/sf/show/a24-x-
 alamo-cinema-club-mandatory-bundle-pearl?cinemaId=0802&sessionId=22087\nDe
 tails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/22/pearl-tickets\nSource: DoThe
 Bay
GEO:37.7562198;-122.419185
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34766190/b4bc297d-975a-4947-89ee-3ef436b41bf9.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003107Z
LOCATION:Alamo Drafthouse Cinema\, 2550 Mission St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 
 94110
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/22/pearl-tickets
END:VEVENT
