 f\nPURPLE RAIN\nAnd\nConcert Film ~ Sign ☮️ The Times\nThursday Decemb
 er 31 New Years Eve!\nDoors Open At 9:00pm\nPurple Music Videos\, Before T
 he Film!\nPurple Rain Starting At 10:00pm\n\nMidnight Countdown With Compl
 imentary Champagne Toast* And Party Favors!\nThen Right Into Sign ☮️ T
 he Times\,\nKeeping The Party Going!\nTickets Are Just $25- And All Ages W
 elcome!\nPurple Rain ~\n“The Kid” (Prince) is a troubled Minneapolis m
 usician. He and his band\, The Revolution are one of three acts playing at
  a local nightclub\, the First Avenue. The other acts are The Time\, a fun
 k band\, lead by Morris Day and The Modernaires\, a new wave band\, lead b
 y Dez Dickerson.\nAspiring singer Apollonia\, comes to town to try her luc
 k hoping to get hired as singer at the First Avenue. Both “The Kid” an
 d Morris Day are attracted to her and vie for her attention. While a roman
 ce starts to develop between “The Kid” and Apollonia\, she accepts a p
 osition in Morris Day’s new all female group\, Apollonia 6\, to the obvi
 ous dismay of “The Kid”. Will The Kid take the top spot?\nSign ☮️ 
 The Times ~\nMusic legend Prince and his band perform 13 numbers\, most of
  them from his double album\, “Sign ‘o’ the Times.” This is high-e
 nergy stuff: neon signs flash above the stage\, suggesting the honky-tonk 
 district of a big city\, and between numbers there are vignettes of street
  life. Sheila E.\, Boni Boyer and...\n\n$25.00\n\nTickets: https://ticketi
 ng.uswest.veezi.com/purchase/19859?siteToken=qkwymq4me4nthdzzgj9fe08j0r\nD
 etails: https://sf.funcheap.com/3rd-annual-purple-nye-purple-rain-sign-tim
 es-vogue-theatre/\nSource: Funcheap SF
